foundation.question_text:
Water is to be piped from a central reservoir $R$ to five surrounding towns $A, B, C, D, E$.
The network diagram shows the possible pipeline routes with distances marked in kilometres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (R) at (0,2);
\coordinate (A) at (2,3.5);
\coordinate (B) at (4.5,3.5);
\coordinate (C) at (6,2);
\coordinate (D) at (4.5,0.5);
\coordinate (E) at (2,0.5);
\draw (R) -- (A) node[midway, above left] {$7$};
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above] {$6$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above right] {$8$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, below right] {$9$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, below] {$7$};
\draw (E) -- (R) node[midway, below left] {$8$};
\draw (A) -- (E) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$10$};
\draw (B) -- (D) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$11$};
\fill (R) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$R$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Determine the shortest total length of water pipe required to connect all five towns to the reservoir.

Five regional health clinics $H_1, H_2, H_3, H_4, H_5$ need to be connected with high-speed data cables.
The network diagram shows the possible cable routes and their lengths in kilometres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (H1) at (0,1.5);
\coordinate (H2) at (2,3);
\coordinate (H3) at (4.5,3);
\coordinate (H4) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (H5) at (2,0);
\draw (H1) -- (H2) node[midway, above left] {$4$};
\draw (H2) -- (H3) node[midway, above] {$6$};
\draw (H3) -- (H4) node[midway, right] {$7$};
\draw (H4) -- (H5) node[midway, below] {$5$};
\draw (H5) -- (H1) node[midway, below left] {$8$};
\draw (H2) -- (H5) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\fill (H1) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$H_1$};
\fill (H2) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$H_2$};
\fill (H3) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$H_3$};
\fill (H4) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$H_4$};
\fill (H5) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$H_5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the minimum total length of cable required to link all five clinics.

development.question_text:
A Japanese garden is being constructed with footpaths connecting six ponds $A, B, C, D, E, F$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3.5);
\coordinate (C) at (4.5,3.5);
\coordinate (D) at (6,2);
\coordinate (E) at (4.5,0.5);
\coordinate (F) at (2,0.5);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$50$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above] {$40$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, above right] {$60$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, below right] {$30$};
\draw (E) -- (F) node[midway, below] {$70$};
\draw (F) -- (A) node[midway, below left] {$40$};
\draw (B) -- (F) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$20$};
\draw (C) -- (E) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$50$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Distances between ponds are shown in metres. The cost to pave the paths is $\$120$ per metre.
Find the minimum total length of paths and the least cost to connect all six ponds.

The network diagram shows travel distances, in kilometres, between six distribution centres $A, B, C, D, E, F$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3.5);
\coordinate (C) at (4.5,3.5);
\coordinate (D) at (6,2);
\coordinate (E) at (4.5,0.5);
\coordinate (F) at (2,0.5);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$6$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above] {$5$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, above right] {$7$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, below right] {$4$};
\draw (E) -- (F) node[midway, below] {$6$};
\draw (F) -- (A) node[midway, below left] {$5$};
\draw (B) -- (F) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\draw (C) -- (E) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find (a) the minimum spanning tree total length to connect all centres, and (b) the shortest travel path between $A$ and $D$. State whether this shortest path is fully contained on the minimum spanning tree.

An alpine road network connecting six mountain villages is blocked by snow.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3.5);
\coordinate (C) at (4.5,3.5);
\coordinate (D) at (6,2);
\coordinate (E) at (4.5,0.5);
\coordinate (F) at (2,0.5);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$8$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above] {$6$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, above right] {$9$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, below right] {$5$};
\draw (E) -- (F) node[midway, below] {$7$};
\draw (F) -- (A) node[midway, below left] {$6$};
\draw (B) -- (F) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\draw (C) -- (E) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Road $BF$ ($4\text{ km}$) has already been cleared by a local snowplow.
Find the minimum additional length of road that must be cleared so every village is accessible from every other village.

A polar expedition connects seven scientific field pods with heating conduits.
The network diagram shows the candidate conduits and their lengths in metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3.5);
\coordinate (C) at (4.5,3.5);
\coordinate (D) at (6,2);
\coordinate (E) at (4.5,0.5);
\coordinate (F) at (2,0.5);
\coordinate (G) at (3,2);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$35$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above] {$30$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, above right] {$40$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, below right] {$25$};
\draw (E) -- (F) node[midway, below] {$35$};
\draw (F) -- (A) node[midway, below left] {$30$};
\draw (A) -- (G) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$20$};
\draw (G) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$25$};
\draw (G) -- (E) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$15$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$F$};
\fill (G) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$G$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Calculate the minimum total length of heating conduit needed to connect all seven pods.

mastery.question_text:
The diagram shows a road network connecting seven towns $A, B, C, D, E, F, G$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3.5);
\coordinate (C) at (4.5,3.5);
\coordinate (D) at (6,2);
\coordinate (E) at (4.5,0.5);
\coordinate (F) at (2,0.5);
\coordinate (G) at (3,2);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$14$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above] {$11$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, above right] {$16$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, below right] {$9$};
\draw (E) -- (F) node[midway, below] {$13$};
\draw (F) -- (A) node[midway, below left] {$12$};
\draw (A) -- (G) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$8$};
\draw (G) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$10$};
\draw (G) -- (E) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$6$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$F$};
\fill (G) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$G$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A landslide has blocked several roads. Roads $AG$ ($8\text{ km}$) and $GE$ ($6\text{ km}$) are already cleared.
Determine the minimal additional road distance that must be cleared to connect all seven towns.
